# 40. CORE RULES

```text
RULE 01
Every character must have a unique Character_ID.

RULE 02
Non-Noble characters use Alphabet Name RNG.

RULE 03
Alphabet RNG is available at every recruitable Star.

RULE 04
Star does not determine whether a character is Noble.

RULE 05
Noble / Royal / Imperial characters use Family RNG.

RULE 06
Non-Noble characters normally have Family_ID = NULL.

RULE 07
Race determines the phonetic naming profile.

RULE 08
Purely unreadable random strings are rejected.

RULE 09
Generated names are validated before creation.

RULE 10
Duplicate names are allowed when Character_ID differs.

RULE 11
Name remains permanently attached to Character_ID.

RULE 12
Star Up does not regenerate the name.

RULE 13
Level Up does not regenerate the name.

RULE 14
Hidden Potential does not regenerate the name.

RULE 15
Name RNG uses a stored Seed for reproducibility.

RULE 16
Character Name is data stored in the Character Database.

RULE 17
Family Name and Commoner Name are separate systems.

RULE 18
Alphabet RNG must follow Core World Building and Race identity.
```

# 41. SYSTEM CONNECTION

```text
RECRUIT SYSTEM
      │
      ▼
CHARACTER RNG
      │
      ├── Race System
      │
      ├── Gender System
      │
      ├── Star System
      │
      ├── Background System
      │
      └── Noble Status RNG
                │
          ┌─────┴─────┐
          ▼           ▼
      NOBLE        NON-NOBLE
          │           │
          ▼           ▼
     FAMILY RNG   ALPHABET RNG
          │           │
          └─────┬─────┘
                ▼
         CHARACTER SYSTEM
                │
                ▼
          CHARACTER_ID
                │
                ▼
            DATABASE
```

Dengan sistem ini, karakter rakyat biasa dapat memiliki **nama yang benar-benar dihasilkan oleh RNG**, tetapi tetap terasa berasal dari ras dan budaya yang sesuai dengan **Core World Building**. Sementara karakter bangsawan tetap menggunakan sistem **Family_ID + Family Name**, sehingga kedua sistem nama tidak bercampur.
